    "description": "Gemini is a utility-scale solar and battery storage project located in Clark County, Nevada. Its customer base is the Nevada power market and contracted offtakers that purchase output and capacity from one of the largest co-located solar-plus-storage assets in the country. The project follows an asset-heavy contracted operating model centered on long-lived generation and storage infrastructure. Public disclosures describe approximately 690 megawatts of solar capacity paired with 380 megawatts of battery storage, with the project representing one of the largest solar-plus-storage installations in the United States. The asset reached full commercial operations in 2024 after construction and financing by Quinbrook and Primergy. APG acquired a 49% interest on behalf of ABP in 2022, and Quinbrook's Valley of Fire fund acquired the remaining 51% in 2024.",
